data: {
    "logs": "\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udccb Task Started \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Task Started                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  Name: Based on the Architect's design, implement the Terraform project:     \u2502\n\u2502  azure-aks-public-cluster-modern.                                            \u2502\n\u2502  --- ARCHITECTURE DESIGN ---                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  PROJECT_SLUG: azure-aks-public-cluster-modern                               \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ```mermaid                                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  graph TD                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      User[User / DevOps] -->|HTTPS/443| AKS[Azure Kubernetes                 \u2502\n\u2502  Service<br/>AKS Cluster<br/>Public Endpoint]                                \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Pull Images| ACR[Azure Container Registry<br/>Managed Identity  \u2502\n\u2502  Access]                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Logs/Metrics| LAWS[Log Analytics Workspace<br/>Container        \u2502\n\u2502  Insights]                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502      VNet[Virtual Network] --> Subnet1[Subnet 1<br/>Availability Zone        \u2502\n\u2502  1<br/>AKS Node Pool]                                                        \u2502\n\u2502      VNet --> Subnet2[Subnet 2<br/>Availability Zone 2<br/>NAT Gateway]      \u2502\n\u2502      Subnet1 --> AKS                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      Subnet2 --> NAT[NAT Gateway<br/>Outbound Internet Access]               \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Pods| Subnet1                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### Terraform Configuration                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 1. `versions.tf`                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    required_version = \">= 1.6.0\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    required_providers {                                                      \u2502\n\u2502      azurerm = {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/azurerm\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502        version = \">= 4.0.0\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502      kubernetes = {                                                          \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/kubernetes\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502        version = \">= 2.0.0\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 2. `provider.tf`                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    backend \"local\" {                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      path = \"./terraform.tfstate\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"azurerm\" {                                                        \u2502\n\u2502    features {}                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"kubernetes\" {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    host                   =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].host                         \u2502\n\u2502    client_certificate     =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].client_certifi  \u2502\n\u2502  cate)                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    client_key             =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].client_key)     \u2502\n\u2502    cluster_ca_certificate =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].cluster_ca_cer  \u2502\n\u2502  tificate)                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 3. `variables.tf`                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"location\" {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Azure region for resources\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"East US\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"resource_group_name\" {                                            \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Name of the resource group\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"rg-aks-prod\"                                               \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"vnet_address_space\" {                                             \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Address space for the Virtual Network\"                     \u2502\n\u2502    type        = list(string)                                                \u2502\n\u2502    default     = [\"10.0.0.0/16\"]                                             \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"subnet_prefixes\" {                                                \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Subnet address prefixes\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    type        = list(string)                                                \u2502\n\u2502    default     = [\"10.0.1.0/24\", \"10.0.2.0/24\"]                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"k8s_version\" {                                                    \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Kubernetes version for AKS\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = null # Will pull latest stable                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"acr_sku\" {                                                        \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"ACR SKU\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"Premium\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"tags\" {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Common tags for all resources\"                             \u2502\n\u2502    type        = map(string)                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    default     = {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      Environment = \"Production\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502      ManagedBy   = \"Terraform\"                                               \u2502\n\u2502      Project     = \"AKS-Public-Cluster\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 4. `main.tf`                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  # Data source for latest stable AKS version                                 \u2502\n\u2502  data \"azurerm_kubernetes_versions\" \"latest\" {                               \u2502\n\u2502    location = var.location                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Resource Group                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_resource_group\" \"main\" {                                  \u2502\n\u2502    name     = var.resource_group_name                                        \u2502\n\u2502    location = var.location                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    tags     = var.tags                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Virtual Network and Subnets (2 AZs)                                       \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_virtual_network\" \"main\" {                                 \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"vnet-aks-main\"                                     \u2502\n\u2502    address_space       = var.vnet_address_space                              \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet\" \"aks_subnet\" {                                    \u2502\n\u2502    count                   = 2                                               \u2502\n\u2502    name                    = \"subnet-aks-${count.index}\"                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name     = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                \u2502\n\u2502    virtual_network_name    = azurerm_virtual_network.main.name               \u2502\n\u2502    address_prefixes        = [var.subnet_prefixes[count.index]]              \u2502\n\u2502    enforce_private_link_endpoint_network_policies = false                    \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # NAT Gateway for Outbound                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway\" \"main\" {                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"nat-gateway-aks\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    sku_name            = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway_public_ip\" \"main\" {                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"nat-gateway-pip-aks\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    sku                 = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    allocation_method   = \"Static\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway_association\" \"main\" {                         \u2502\n\u2502    nat_gateway_id = azurerm_nat_gateway.main.id                              \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[1].id                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Route Table                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_route_table\" \"main\" {                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"rt-aks-internal\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_route\" \"main\" {                                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                   = \"route-internet\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    address_prefix         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    route_table_id         = azurerm_route_table.main.id                      \u2502\n\u2502    next_hop_type          = \"VirtualAppliance\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    next_hop_in_ip_address = azurerm_nat_gateway.main.private_ip_address      \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet_route_table_association\" \"main\" {                  \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[1].id                          \u2502\n\u2502    route_table_id = azurerm_route_table.main.id                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # NSGs                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_group\" \"main\" {                          \u2502\n\u2502    count             = 2                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name              = \"nsg-aks-subnet-${count.index}\"                       \u2502\n\u2502    location          = var.location                                          \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags              = var.tags                                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main\" {                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowSSH\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1001                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"22\"                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main_http\" {                      \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowHTTP\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1002                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"80\"                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main_https\" {                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowHTTPS\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1003                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"443\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association\" \"main\" {       \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[count.index].id                \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_id =                                               \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].id                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Azure Container Registry                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_container_registry\" \"main\" {                              \u2502\n\u2502    name                     = \"acraksprod001\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name      = azurerm_resource_group.main.name               \u2502\n\u2502    location                 = var.location                                   \u2502\n\u2502    sku                      = var.acr_sku                                    \u2502\n\u2502    admin_enabled            = false                                          \u2502\n\u2502    tags                     = var.tags                                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Log Analytics Workspace                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_log_analytics_workspace\" \"main\" {                         \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"law-aks-prod\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    sku                 = \"PerGB2018\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502    retention_in_days   = 30                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_monitor_container_insights\" \"main\" {                      \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    workspace_id        = azurerm_log_analytics_workspace.main.id             \u2502\n\u2502    cluster_name        = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.name                \u2502\n\u2502    kubernetes_version  = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kubernetes_version  \u2502\n\u2502    depends_on          = [azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main]                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # AKS Cluster                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_kubernetes_cluster\" \"main\" {                              \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"aks-prod-cluster\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    dns_prefix          = \"aksprod\"                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    linux_profile {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      admin_username = \"azureuser\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      ssh_key {                                                               \u2502\n\u2502        key_data = file(\"~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub\")                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    network_profile {                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      network_plugin     = \"azure\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502      load_balancer_sku = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    addon_profile {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      oms_agent {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502        enabled    = true                                                     \u2502\n\u2502        log_analytics_workspace_resource_id =                                 \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_log_analytics_workspace.main.id                                     \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    identity {                                                                \u2502\n\u2502      type         = \"SystemAssigned\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    oidc_issuer_profile {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      enabled = true                                                          \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    workload_identity_enabled = true                                          \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    api_profile {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502      version = \"2023-08-01\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    azure_radial_dns_prefix_enabled = false                                   \u2502\n\u2502    default_node_pool {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502      name            = \"systempool\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502      node_count      = 2                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      vm_size         = \"Standard_D16s_v5\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502      os_disk_size_gb = 128                                                   \u2502\n\u2502      vnet_subnet_id  = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[0].id                       \u2502\n\u2502      zones           = [\"1\", \"2\"] # Requested multi-az                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    tags = var.tags                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    lifecycle {                                                               \u2502\n\u2502      ignore_changes = [                                                      \u2502\n\u2502        default_node_pool[0].node_count                                       \u2502\n\u2502      ]                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # AKS Node Pool (Autoscaling)                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_kubernetes_node_pool\" \"autoscaling\" {                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                  = \"autoscalingpool\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    kubernetes_cluster_id = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.id                \u2502\n\u2502    node_count            = 2 # Initial count                                 \u2502\n\u2502    vm_size               = \"Standard_D16s_v5\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    os_disk_size_gb       = 128                                               \u2502\n\u2502    vnet_subnet_id        = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[0].id                   \u2502\n\u2502    zones                 = [\"1\", \"2\"]                                        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    enable_auto_scaling = true                                                \u2502\n\u2502    min_count           = 2                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    max_count           = 5                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    os_sku               = \"UbuntuLTS\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    mode                 = \"User\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    tags = var.tags                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Role Assignment: AKS to ACR                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_role_assignment\" \"main\" {                                 \u2502\n\u2502    scope                = azurerm_container_registry.main.id                 \u2502\n\u2502    role_definition_name = \"AcrPull\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    principal_id         =                                                    \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.identity[0].principal_id                    \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 5. `outputs.tf`                                                        \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  output \"cluster_name\" {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The name of the AKS cluster\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    value       = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.name                        \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"cluster_kube_config\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Base64 encoded kubeconfig file\"                            \u2502\n\u2502    value       =                                                             \u2502\n\u2502  base64encode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config_raw)               \u2502\n\u2502    sensitive   = true                                                        \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"acr_login_server\" {                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The ACR login server URI\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    value       = azurerm_container_registry.main.login_server                \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"oidc_issuer_url\" {                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The OIDC issuer URL of the cluster\"                        \u2502\n\u2502    value       =                                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.oidc_issuer_profile[0].issuer_url           \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  ---------------------------                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## MANDATORY RULES (FAILURE TO FOLLOW = BROKEN CODE)                        \u2502\n\u2502  1. You MUST use the `Write Terraform File` tool for EVERY SINGLE FILE you   \u2502\n\u2502  create.                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  2. DO NOT WRITE PLAIN TEXT TERRAFORM. YOU MUST CALL THE TOOL.               \u2502\n\u2502  3. If you need to create 15 files, you MUST call the tool 15 times.         \u2502\n\u2502  4. If a \"PREVIOUS ROUND FAILED\" block is present, you MUST prioritize       \u2502\n\u2502  correcting the reported errors and applying the provided KNOWN FIX          \u2502\n\u2502  GUIDANCE or reflection advice. You MUST override the Architect design if    \u2502\n\u2502  it contradicts the required fix (e.g. if the design specifies               \u2502\n\u2502  \"enable_auto_scaling = true\" but the guidance instructs to rename it to     \u2502\n\u2502  \"auto_scaling_enabled = true\", you MUST apply the rename).                  \u2502\n\u2502  5. Structure: Root `main.tf` calling modules in `modules/` directory.       \u2502\n\u2502     Module sources MUST be relative path strings (e.g., source =             \u2502\n\u2502  \"./modules/vpc\").                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  6. You MUST create a `README.md` in the project ROOT.                       \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## HCL FORMATTING (CRITICAL)                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - NEVER use semicolons (;) to separate arguments. Use NEWLINES.             \u2502\n\u2502  - Every resource argument MUST be on its own line.                          \u2502\n\u2502  - Every closing brace } MUST be on its own line.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - BAD:  resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id; cidr_block   \u2502\n\u2502  = \"10.0.1.0/24\" }                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - GOOD:                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502      vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id                                            \u2502\n\u2502      cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## REQUIRED FILES                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - Root files: Define the `terraform { required_providers { } }` block and   \u2502\n\u2502  `provider` block exactly once (e.g. in `versions.tf` or `main.tf`). DO NOT  \u2502\n\u2502  duplicate provider blocks across multiple files.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `variables.tf`: Input variables (e.g., region).                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `outputs.tf`: Key outputs (endpoints, IDs, ARNs).                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## EKS / INFRASTRUCTURE COMPLETENESS CHECKLIST                              \u2502\n\u2502  If creating EKS, you MUST include ALL of the following:                     \u2502\n\u2502  - At least 2 subnets across 2 different Availability Zones (EKS requires    \u2502\n\u2502  this).                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets must have `map_public_ip_on_launch = true` for public clusters.   \u2502\n\u2502  - IAM roles MUST have `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resources:           \u2502\n\u2502    * Cluster role: AmazonEKSClusterPolicy                                    \u2502\n\u2502    * Node role: AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy,                                   \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly, AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy                    \u2502\n\u2502  - EKS `vpc_config` must include `endpoint_public_access = true` for public  \u2502\n\u2502  clusters.                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  - Node group must have `depends_on` referencing the IAM policy              \u2502\n\u2502  attachments.                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets should be tagged: `kubernetes.io/cluster/<name> = shared`.        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Project Slug: azure-aks-public-cluster-modern                               \u2502\n\u2502  ID: 3f79676b-44b3-4b07-a1e6-0121490430d6                                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \ud83e\udd16 Agent Started \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Agent: Senior Terraform Developer                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Task: Based on the Architect's design, implement the Terraform project:     \u2502\n\u2502  azure-aks-public-cluster-modern.                                            \u2502\n\u2502  --- ARCHITECTURE DESIGN ---                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  PROJECT_SLUG: azure-aks-public-cluster-modern                               \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ```mermaid                                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  graph TD                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      User[User / DevOps] -->|HTTPS/443| AKS[Azure Kubernetes                 \u2502\n\u2502  Service<br/>AKS Cluster<br/>Public Endpoint]                                \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Pull Images| ACR[Azure Container Registry<br/>Managed Identity  \u2502\n\u2502  Access]                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Logs/Metrics| LAWS[Log Analytics Workspace<br/>Container        \u2502\n\u2502  Insights]                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502      VNet[Virtual Network] --> Subnet1[Subnet 1<br/>Availability Zone        \u2502\n\u2502  1<br/>AKS Node Pool]                                                        \u2502\n\u2502      VNet --> Subnet2[Subnet 2<br/>Availability Zone 2<br/>NAT Gateway]      \u2502\n\u2502      Subnet1 --> AKS                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      Subnet2 --> NAT[NAT Gateway<br/>Outbound Internet Access]               \u2502\n\u2502      AKS -->|Pods| Subnet1                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### Terraform Configuration                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 1. `versions.tf`                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    required_version = \">= 1.6.0\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    required_providers {                                                      \u2502\n\u2502      azurerm = {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/azurerm\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502        version = \">= 4.0.0\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502      kubernetes = {                                                          \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/kubernetes\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502        version = \">= 2.0.0\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 2. `provider.tf`                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    backend \"local\" {                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      path = \"./terraform.tfstate\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"azurerm\" {                                                        \u2502\n\u2502    features {}                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"kubernetes\" {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    host                   =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].host                         \u2502\n\u2502    client_certificate     =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].client_certifi  \u2502\n\u2502  cate)                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    client_key             =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].client_key)     \u2502\n\u2502    cluster_ca_certificate =                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  base64decode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config[0].cluster_ca_cer  \u2502\n\u2502  tificate)                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 3. `variables.tf`                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"location\" {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Azure region for resources\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"East US\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"resource_group_name\" {                                            \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Name of the resource group\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"rg-aks-prod\"                                               \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"vnet_address_space\" {                                             \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Address space for the Virtual Network\"                     \u2502\n\u2502    type        = list(string)                                                \u2502\n\u2502    default     = [\"10.0.0.0/16\"]                                             \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"subnet_prefixes\" {                                                \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Subnet address prefixes\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    type        = list(string)                                                \u2502\n\u2502    default     = [\"10.0.1.0/24\", \"10.0.2.0/24\"]                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"k8s_version\" {                                                    \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Kubernetes version for AKS\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = null # Will pull latest stable                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"acr_sku\" {                                                        \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"ACR SKU\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    type        = string                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    default     = \"Premium\"                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  variable \"tags\" {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Common tags for all resources\"                             \u2502\n\u2502    type        = map(string)                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    default     = {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      Environment = \"Production\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502      ManagedBy   = \"Terraform\"                                               \u2502\n\u2502      Project     = \"AKS-Public-Cluster\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 4. `main.tf`                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  # Data source for latest stable AKS version                                 \u2502\n\u2502  data \"azurerm_kubernetes_versions\" \"latest\" {                               \u2502\n\u2502    location = var.location                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Resource Group                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_resource_group\" \"main\" {                                  \u2502\n\u2502    name     = var.resource_group_name                                        \u2502\n\u2502    location = var.location                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    tags     = var.tags                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Virtual Network and Subnets (2 AZs)                                       \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_virtual_network\" \"main\" {                                 \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"vnet-aks-main\"                                     \u2502\n\u2502    address_space       = var.vnet_address_space                              \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet\" \"aks_subnet\" {                                    \u2502\n\u2502    count                   = 2                                               \u2502\n\u2502    name                    = \"subnet-aks-${count.index}\"                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name     = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                \u2502\n\u2502    virtual_network_name    = azurerm_virtual_network.main.name               \u2502\n\u2502    address_prefixes        = [var.subnet_prefixes[count.index]]              \u2502\n\u2502    enforce_private_link_endpoint_network_policies = false                    \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # NAT Gateway for Outbound                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway\" \"main\" {                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"nat-gateway-aks\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    sku_name            = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway_public_ip\" \"main\" {                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"nat-gateway-pip-aks\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    sku                 = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    allocation_method   = \"Static\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_nat_gateway_association\" \"main\" {                         \u2502\n\u2502    nat_gateway_id = azurerm_nat_gateway.main.id                              \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[1].id                          \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Route Table                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_route_table\" \"main\" {                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"rt-aks-internal\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_route\" \"main\" {                                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                   = \"route-internet\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    address_prefix         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    route_table_id         = azurerm_route_table.main.id                      \u2502\n\u2502    next_hop_type          = \"VirtualAppliance\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    next_hop_in_ip_address = azurerm_nat_gateway.main.private_ip_address      \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet_route_table_association\" \"main\" {                  \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[1].id                          \u2502\n\u2502    route_table_id = azurerm_route_table.main.id                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # NSGs                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_group\" \"main\" {                          \u2502\n\u2502    count             = 2                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    name              = \"nsg-aks-subnet-${count.index}\"                       \u2502\n\u2502    location          = var.location                                          \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    tags              = var.tags                                              \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main\" {                           \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowSSH\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1001                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"22\"                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main_http\" {                      \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowHTTP\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1002                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"80\"                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_network_security_rule\" \"main_https\" {                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                        = \"AllowHTTPS\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    priority                    = 1003                                        \u2502\n\u2502    direction                   = \"Inbound\"                                   \u2502\n\u2502    access                       = \"Allow\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502    protocol                     = \"Tcp\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_port_range            = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_port_range       = \"443\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    source_address_prefix        = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    destination_address_prefix   = \"*\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name         = azurerm_resource_group.main.name            \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_name =                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].name                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_subnet_network_security_group_association\" \"main\" {       \u2502\n\u2502    subnet_id      = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[count.index].id                \u2502\n\u2502    network_security_group_id =                                               \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_network_security_group.main[count.index].id                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Azure Container Registry                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_container_registry\" \"main\" {                              \u2502\n\u2502    name                     = \"acraksprod001\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name      = azurerm_resource_group.main.name               \u2502\n\u2502    location                 = var.location                                   \u2502\n\u2502    sku                      = var.acr_sku                                    \u2502\n\u2502    admin_enabled            = false                                          \u2502\n\u2502    tags                     = var.tags                                       \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Log Analytics Workspace                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_log_analytics_workspace\" \"main\" {                         \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"law-aks-prod\"                                      \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    sku                 = \"PerGB2018\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502    retention_in_days   = 30                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    tags                = var.tags                                            \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_monitor_container_insights\" \"main\" {                      \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    workspace_id        = azurerm_log_analytics_workspace.main.id             \u2502\n\u2502    cluster_name        = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.name                \u2502\n\u2502    kubernetes_version  = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kubernetes_version  \u2502\n\u2502    depends_on          = [azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main]                   \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # AKS Cluster                                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_kubernetes_cluster\" \"main\" {                              \u2502\n\u2502    name                = \"aks-prod-cluster\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    location            = var.location                                        \u2502\n\u2502    resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.main.name                    \u2502\n\u2502    dns_prefix          = \"aksprod\"                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    linux_profile {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      admin_username = \"azureuser\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      ssh_key {                                                               \u2502\n\u2502        key_data = file(\"~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub\")                                  \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    network_profile {                                                         \u2502\n\u2502      network_plugin     = \"azure\"                                            \u2502\n\u2502      load_balancer_sku = \"Standard\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    addon_profile {                                                           \u2502\n\u2502      oms_agent {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502        enabled    = true                                                     \u2502\n\u2502        log_analytics_workspace_resource_id =                                 \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_log_analytics_workspace.main.id                                     \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    identity {                                                                \u2502\n\u2502      type         = \"SystemAssigned\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    oidc_issuer_profile {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      enabled = true                                                          \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    workload_identity_enabled = true                                          \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    api_profile {                                                             \u2502\n\u2502      version = \"2023-08-01\"                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    azure_radial_dns_prefix_enabled = false                                   \u2502\n\u2502    default_node_pool {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502      name            = \"systempool\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502      node_count      = 2                                                     \u2502\n\u2502      vm_size         = \"Standard_D16s_v5\"                                    \u2502\n\u2502      os_disk_size_gb = 128                                                   \u2502\n\u2502      vnet_subnet_id  = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[0].id                       \u2502\n\u2502      zones           = [\"1\", \"2\"] # Requested multi-az                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    tags = var.tags                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    lifecycle {                                                               \u2502\n\u2502      ignore_changes = [                                                      \u2502\n\u2502        default_node_pool[0].node_count                                       \u2502\n\u2502      ]                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # AKS Node Pool (Autoscaling)                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_kubernetes_node_pool\" \"autoscaling\" {                     \u2502\n\u2502    name                  = \"autoscalingpool\"                                 \u2502\n\u2502    kubernetes_cluster_id = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.id                \u2502\n\u2502    node_count            = 2 # Initial count                                 \u2502\n\u2502    vm_size               = \"Standard_D16s_v5\"                                \u2502\n\u2502    os_disk_size_gb       = 128                                               \u2502\n\u2502    vnet_subnet_id        = azurerm_subnet.aks_subnet[0].id                   \u2502\n\u2502    zones                 = [\"1\", \"2\"]                                        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    enable_auto_scaling = true                                                \u2502\n\u2502    min_count           = 2                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    max_count           = 5                                                   \u2502\n\u2502    os_sku               = \"UbuntuLTS\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502    mode                 = \"User\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    tags = var.tags                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  # Role Assignment: AKS to ACR                                               \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"azurerm_role_assignment\" \"main\" {                                 \u2502\n\u2502    scope                = azurerm_container_registry.main.id                 \u2502\n\u2502    role_definition_name = \"AcrPull\"                                          \u2502\n\u2502    principal_id         =                                                    \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.identity[0].principal_id                    \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  #### 5. `outputs.tf`                                                        \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  output \"cluster_name\" {                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The name of the AKS cluster\"                               \u2502\n\u2502    value       = azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.name                        \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"cluster_kube_config\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"Base64 encoded kubeconfig file\"                            \u2502\n\u2502    value       =                                                             \u2502\n\u2502  base64encode(azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.kube_config_raw)               \u2502\n\u2502    sensitive   = true                                                        \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"acr_login_server\" {                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The ACR login server URI\"                                  \u2502\n\u2502    value       = azurerm_container_registry.main.login_server                \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  output \"oidc_issuer_url\" {                                                  \u2502\n\u2502    description = \"The OIDC issuer URL of the cluster\"                        \u2502\n\u2502    value       =                                                             \u2502\n\u2502  azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.main.oidc_issuer_profile[0].issuer_url           \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  ---------------------------                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## MANDATORY RULES (FAILURE TO FOLLOW = BROKEN CODE)                        \u2502\n\u2502  1. You MUST use the `Write Terraform File` tool for EVERY SINGLE FILE you   \u2502\n\u2502  create.                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  2. DO NOT WRITE PLAIN TEXT TERRAFORM. YOU MUST CALL THE TOOL.               \u2502\n\u2502  3. If you need to create 15 files, you MUST call the tool 15 times.         \u2502\n\u2502  4. If a \"PREVIOUS ROUND FAILED\" block is present, you MUST prioritize       \u2502\n\u2502  correcting the reported errors and applying the provided KNOWN FIX          \u2502\n\u2502  GUIDANCE or reflection advice. You MUST override the Architect design if    \u2502\n\u2502  it contradicts the required fix (e.g. if the design specifies               \u2502\n\u2502  \"enable_auto_scaling = true\" but the guidance instructs to rename it to     \u2502\n\u2502  \"auto_scaling_enabled = true\", you MUST apply the rename).                  \u2502\n\u2502  5. Structure: Root `main.tf` calling modules in `modules/` directory.       \u2502\n\u2502     Module sources MUST be relative path strings (e.g., source =             \u2502\n\u2502  \"./modules/vpc\").                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  6. You MUST create a `README.md` in the project ROOT.                       \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## HCL FORMATTING (CRITICAL)                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - NEVER use semicolons (;) to separate arguments. Use NEWLINES.             \u2502\n\u2502  - Every resource argument MUST be on its own line.                          \u2502\n\u2502  - Every closing brace } MUST be on its own line.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - BAD:  resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id; cidr_block   \u2502\n\u2502  = \"10.0.1.0/24\" }                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - GOOD:                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502      vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id                                            \u2502\n\u2502      cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## REQUIRED FILES                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - Root files: Define the `terraform { required_providers { } }` block and   \u2502\n\u2502  `provider` block exactly once (e.g. in `versions.tf` or `main.tf`). DO NOT  \u2502\n\u2502  duplicate provider blocks across multiple files.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `variables.tf`: Input variables (e.g., region).                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `outputs.tf`: Key outputs (endpoints, IDs, ARNs).                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## EKS / INFRASTRUCTURE COMPLETENESS CHECKLIST                              \u2502\n\u2502  If creating EKS, you MUST include ALL of the following:                     \u2502\n\u2502  - At least 2 subnets across 2 different Availability Zones (EKS requires    \u2502\n\u2502  this).                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets must have `map_public_ip_on_launch = true` for public clusters.   \u2502\n\u2502  - IAM roles MUST have `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resources:           \u2502\n\u2502    * Cluster role: AmazonEKSClusterPolicy                                    \u2502\n\u2502    * Node role: AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy,                                   \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly, AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy                    \u2502\n\u2502  - EKS `vpc_config` must include `endpoint_public_access = true` for public  \u2502\n\u2502  clusters.                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  - Node group must have `depends_on` referencing the IAM policy              \u2502\n\u2502  attachments.                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets should be tagged: `kubernetes.io/cluster/<name> = shared`.        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Project Slug: azure-aks-public-cluster-modern                               \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u001b[92m18:09:43 - LiteLLM:WARNING\u001b[0m: utils.py:768 - `litellm.set_verbose` is deprecated. Please set `os.environ['LITELLM_LOG'] = 'DEBUG'` for debug logs.\nInitialized litellm callbacks, Async Success Callbacks: []\nSYNC kwargs[caching]: False; litellm.cache: None; kwargs.get('cache')['no-cache']: False\nFinal returned optional params: {'temperature': 0.7, 'stream': False, 'max_retries': 5, 'extra_body': {}}\n"
